<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Goiás Velho</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Vila Boa, Goiás</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Goiás Velho, founded in 1727 as Vila Boa de Goiás during the gold rush of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, was the capital of the Captaincy of Goiás and later of the state of Goiás until 1937, when the capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goiania">Goiânia</a>. Its colonial churches and streets were declared a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 2001.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/goias-velho.jpg" alt="Goiás Velho" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antônio Ricardo Gomes de Souza · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Largo_do_Jardim_ao_Largo_do_Ros%C3%A1rio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
